.\" Manual page of amcset. Part of AMCSET (GPL-3.0-or-later).
.TH AMCSET 1 "@AMCSET_RELEASE_DATE@" "AMCSET @PROJECT_VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
amcset \- Monte Carlo transport of ions in matter and the radiation damage they cause
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B amcset run
.I scenario.json
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B amcset trim
.I TRIM.IN
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B amcset validate
.IR scenario.json | TRIM.IN
.br
.B amcset convert
.I in out
.br
.B amcset stopping
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B amcset elements
.RI [ symbol | Z ...]
.br
.B amcset cell
.IR file " | " \fB\-\-structure\fP " " NAME
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B amcset template
.RB [ srim | native ]
.RB [ \-o
.IR FILE ]
.br
.B amcset version
|
.B help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B amcset
is the command-line program of AMCSET, a Monte Carlo simulator of ion (and
electron) transport and radiation damage in layered amorphous and
crystalline targets. Its SRIM mode reproduces SRIM-2013's TRIM: it reads
TRIM.IN and TRIM.DAT, writes TRIM's output files as well as CSV, JSON and
Parquet tables, and uses the SRIM-2013 stopping tables that come with it.
A calculation is described by a scenario file (JSON); options override its
keys. The graphical program is
.BR amcset\-gui (1).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B run
Run a scenario (SRIM mode or the native engine).
.TP
.B trim
Run a TRIM batch input (TRIM.IN) in SRIM mode.
.TP
.B validate
Check a scenario or TRIM.IN without running it.
.TP
.B convert
Convert between TRIM.IN and scenario JSON.
.TP
.B stopping
Electronic and nuclear stopping powers and ranges (like SRIM's SR Module).
.TP
.B elements
Element data: masses, densities, surface binding energies, ionization potentials.
.TP
.B cell
A crystal's unit cell from a file (CIF, POSCAR, LAMMPS data, extended XYZ) or
a built-in structure: summary, conversion, the scenario's crystal object, beam
directions.
.TP
.B template
Print or save an example scenario.
.SH OPTIONS
The most used options of
.BR run ,
.B trim
and
.BR validate ;
.B amcset help
lists every option of every command.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " " \fIDIR\fP
Output directory.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-ions " " \fIN\fP
Number of incident ions.
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-threads " " \fIN\fP
Worker threads (default: all cores). Results do not depend on it.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-seed " " \fIS\fP
Random number seed: the same seed gives the same results.
.TP
.BR \-\-damage " " kp | full | monolayer
Quick (Kinchin-Pease) damage, full cascades, or monolayer collisions.
.TP
.BI \-\-set " KEY=VALUE"
Override any scenario key, e.g.
.B \-\-set
"ion.energy=2 MeV" (repeatable). Physical values take units.
.TP
.BI \-\-formats " LIST"
Output formats: any of trim, csv, json, parquet.
.TP
.B \-\-fix\-trim\-bugs
Correct every bug of TRIM.exe that SRIM mode reproduces.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
No progress bar.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Engine messages and the diagnostic log on standard error.
.TP
.BI \-\-log " FILE"
Write the diagnostic log to FILE.
.SH SIGNALS
SIGINT (Ctrl+C), SIGTERM and SIGHUP stop a running calculation after the ions
in progress; the results so far are written, then the program ends by the
same signal (the shell reports 128 plus the signal number, 130 for SIGINT).
A second signal ends the program at once. Other signals keep their default
actions.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
An error in the scenario, the input files or the run.
.TP
.B 2
A usage error (unknown command or option).
.TP
.B 3
A crash; a crash report was written (its path is printed).
.TP
.B 128+n
The run was interrupted by signal
.I n
(see SIGNALS).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B AMCSET_DATA_DIR
A directory with the stopping tables (srim2013/srim2013_stopping.amcset),
searched before the installed ones.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/amcset/srim2013/
The bundled SRIM-2013 stopping tables (the path follows the installation
prefix).
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/amcset/
Documentation: the scenario keys (docs/CLI.md), the output files
(docs/OUTPUT.md), SRIM mode and its validation (docs/SRIM_MODE.md).
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
amcset template srim \-o fe.json
amcset run fe.json \-n 10000 \-o out
amcset trim TRIM.IN \-s 101 \-o out
amcset stopping \-\-ion He \-\-target Si \-\-from 10keV \-\-to 10MeV
.fi
